𝒢 (calligraphic G)	 or	𝛄   (gamma)	 for grouping with 	Aggregate function
	example:	gamma a; count(*)->x ( R )
	represents the "group by" operation where you group the tuples in relation "R" based on 
	attribute "a", then aggregate by counting the number of tuples within each group, storing 
	the count in a new attribute named "x" within the resulting relation
	
	order the result by the first column (default is ascending) 
	and the second column descending:  γ a, b ; sum(c)->x ( Customer )

	(NOTE:  If no grouping, then the entire table is the group)


